Verdict: PASS. I judged it from the diff plus one search of src/. I didn't re-run the suite (the harness already had it green) or exercise the fence by hand. The verdict is in session_plan/eval_task_2.md.

• Launch-dir anchor: main now records the launch directory once, before any tool or /cd can run. The fence compares against that instead of the live cwd, and only uses the cwd if nothing was recorded. I searched src/ and found nothing that already stored the launch directory, so adding a new one was justified.
• Fails closed: if there's no anchor at all, every read is asked about instead of allowed. A relative path is refused when the current directory can't be read. The old code allowed both cases silently.
• Tests: they cover all four cases the task asked for:
  • a read after /cd now asks, checked against the old rule;
  • users who never /cd see no change;
  • an approval given before /cd still covers its path after it;
  • with no anchor, it asks instead of allowing.

